---
/*
 * [WEB-REPOSITION-2 2026-08-28] Rewritten from "Never miss a call again", which
 * was a post about the AI receptionist — a feature the 2026-08-27 product pivot
 * is retiring. The URL is kept alive on purpose: it is indexed, and a 404 loses
 * whatever authority it has earned. Same idea ("don't miss the thing that
 * matters"), told about bookings, which is what avaTOK actually sells now.
 *
 * Every claim here is checked against what ships: calendar slots, booking,
 * paid live sessions, wallet, and payout methods. Commission and payout minimums are
 * deliberately NOT quoted as numbers — /pricing-fees and /payouts say they are
 * shown before you commit, and a blog post must not contradict the policy.
 */
export const prerender = true;
import Content from '../../layouts/Content.astro';
---

<Content
  kicker="Blog · Getting booked"
  title="Never miss a booking"
  description="How avaTOK turns your free hours into bookable slots — you publish a listing, open your calendar, and people book the time you actually have."
  lead="Your calendar does the chasing. Open the hours you're free, and let people book them."
  updated="2026-08-28"
>
  <p data-i18n="web-blog.bd51fe25cd794490">
    The hardest part of getting paid for your time is rarely the work itself. It is the
    back-and-forth before it: what do you charge, when are you free, did they actually confirm, and
    are you going to be sitting there at 7pm for someone who never intended to show up.
  </p>
  <p data-i18n="web-blog.cfeda11dc5c35370">
    avaTOK removes that negotiation. You publish what you offer, you mark when you are available,
    and people book a real slot.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-blog.ef25bc55bc9e5ecf">Publish once, get booked repeatedly</h2>
  <p data-i18n="web-blog.158d858a102238a7">
    A listing is the thing people find and buy: a category, a description of what you offer, a
    session length, and a price in tokens (1 token = ₹1). Publishing one is free. It keeps working
    while you are asleep, which is the whole point — you are not answering "are you available
    Thursday?" for the ninth time.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-blog.75402b1a6f28033a">Your calendar is the source of truth</h2>
  <p data-i18n="web-blog.e131fea507ff1140">
    You open the slots you are genuinely free for. Someone books one of those slots or nothing at
    all. There is no double-booking to untangle and no "let me check and get back to you", because
    the answer is already on the screen they are looking at.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-blog.b7cd38924ec5f0fc">The session happens on avaTOK</h2>
  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.4f88cbfdb7d4bf13">When the time comes, the session runs inside avaTOK — a private 1:1 video session, or a paid
    live event people join. Nobody swaps phone numbers, and nobody has to install something else
    ten minutes beforehand. Your real number stays private throughout; see</ui-copy>
    <a data-i18n="web-blog.6d4f8f3dfb235d0b" href="/blog/your-private-number">why you should never hand out your real number</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 data-i18n="web-blog.6f0e3b0033522057">Getting paid is the boring part, and that is the goal</h2>
  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.4b479ec3c05d916e">The customer pays in tokens when they book. Your earnings, less the platform commission shown
    to you before you publish, land in your avaTOK wallet, and you withdraw to a verified payout
    address. The exact fees, taxes and any minimum are shown on screen before you confirm anything —
    see</ui-copy> <a data-i18n="web-blog.5e2a4b33bff1936b" href="/pricing-fees">Pricing &amp; Fees</a> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.6201111b83a0cb5b">and</ui-copy>
    <a data-i18n="web-blog.aba115e7791e41dc" href="/payouts">Payouts &amp; Withdrawals</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <p>
      <strong data-i18n="web-blog.e424a72c45ead7d6">avaTOK is still evolving.</strong> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.6d97890f3b2e5969">We are an early-stage Delaware corporation,
      business, access is invite-only, and our payment gateway application is under review,
      so payments are not yet live to the public.</ui-copy>
      <a data-i18n="web-blog.1e7c107176e052c9" href="/terms#status">Read our full status</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.51d47f3a10496d74">Ready to open your calendar?</ui-copy> <a data-i18n="web-blog.69ca6647394bb064" href="/sign-up">Create a free listing</a> <ui-copy style="display:contents" data-i18n="web-blog.7175517a370b5cd2">or</ui-copy>
    <a data-i18n="web-blog.e0f69d407c135efd" href="/marketplace">see what other creators are offering</a>.
  </p>
</Content>
